<article>
	<h1><span>Shopping Cart: Items Ordered</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#list-filters">List Filters</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists the items in completed shopping cart orders, one row per SKU in each order.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<p>Click the <strong>SKU ID</strong>, <strong>Order ID</strong>, <strong>Order placed</strong> or
			<strong>Purchased by</strong> heading to sort the list by that column. Click it again to reverse the
			order.</p>

		<dl>
			<dt>SKU ID</dt>
			<dd>The SKU's ID number. Click it to edit the SKU in the Storefront component.</dd>

			<dt>Product</dt>
			<dd>The product name, with its SKU on the line below. Click the product name to list only items of that
				product, or the SKU to list only items of that SKU. <em>Product n/a</em> or <em>SKU n/a</em> is shown
				when the name is missing.</dd>

			<dt>QTY</dt>
			<dd>The quantity ordered.</dd>

			<dt>Price</dt>
			<dd>The price recorded for the item in the order.</dd>

			<dt>Order ID</dt>
			<dd>The order's number. Click it to view the order.</dd>

			<dt>Order placed</dt>
			<dd>The date and time the order was last updated.</dd>

			<dt>Purchased by</dt>
			<dd>The name of the member who placed the order. Click it to open the member in the Members component.
				<em>(unknown)</em> is shown when the order has no member name.</dd>
		</dl>

		<p>When the list is limited to one order, a row above the headings shows <em>Order: #</em> and the order
			number. When it is limited to one product or SKU, a row shows <em>Orders of</em> and its name. Each of
			these rows has a <strong>Clear</strong> button.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="list-filters">
		<h2><span>List Filters</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Search</dt>
			<dd>Lists only items whose member name, username, SKU, product name or order ID contains the text.</dd>

			<dt>From &mdash; To</dt>
			<dd>Lists only items from orders placed between these dates. The default is from one month ago to today.
				The dates are ignored while the list is limited to one order.</dd>

			<dt>Update</dt>
			<dd>Applies the filters.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Options window where settings such as default parameters or permissions can be edited.
				Shown only to users who may configure the component.</dd>

			<dt>Download CSV</dt>
			<dd>Downloads a CSV file of the items matching the current search, dates and order filters. Its columns
				are SKU ID, Product, QTY, Price, Order ID, Order Placed, Purchased By and Purchased By (userId).</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Software Downloads</dt>
			<dt>Orders (this page)</dt>
		</dl>
		<p>Below them, a second row of links chooses the report:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>All orders</dt>
			<dt>Items ordered (this page)</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
